WEBVTT

00:00:06.480 --> 00:00:10.610
<i>When we're born, we're given a book.</i>

00:00:11.100 --> 00:00:16.000
<i>A script containing everything about us,
 the meaning of our lives... Everything.</i>

00:00:16.000 --> 00:00:17.120
<i>"The Book of Fate."</i>

00:00:17.710 --> 00:00:25.070
<i>We follow the scripts laid out in 
these books until the day we die.</i>

00:00:32.270 --> 00:00:35.380
<i>So tell me...</i>

00:00:41.970 --> 00:00:45.760
<i>When someone's Book of Fate is filled 
with nothing but blank pages,</i>

00:00:46.420 --> 00:00:50.780
<i>what sort of role, what sort of fate,
 are they expected to play?</i>

00:00:58.390 --> 00:00:59.620
What's wrong?

00:01:02.460 --> 00:01:03.800
Are you hurt?

00:01:04.290 --> 00:01:05.710
No...

00:01:05.710 --> 00:01:08.500
I tripped on my way back from an errand...

00:01:17.370 --> 00:01:19.640
Don't worry. I'll handle it!

00:01:27.340 --> 00:01:29.240
Are you okay?

00:01:29.240 --> 00:01:31.570
Just a little further...

00:01:52.650 --> 00:01:54.160
Thank you!

00:01:54.160 --> 00:01:55.300
Um...

00:01:55.520 --> 00:01:56.880
I'm Ex!

00:01:56.880 --> 00:01:58.870
Thank you, Ex!

00:02:00.220 --> 00:02:01.220
What's your name?

00:02:01.430 --> 00:02:04.300
My name is Cinderella!

00:03:35.860 --> 00:03:41.320
Cinderella of Recollection

00:03:52.280 --> 00:03:53.640
You're late.

00:03:53.640 --> 00:03:54.920
I'm sorry, Uncle...

00:03:55.270 --> 00:03:56.490
No...

00:03:57.110 --> 00:03:58.140
Oh, right!

00:03:58.140 --> 00:04:00.210
These are supposed to be 
delivered to town, right?

00:04:00.470 --> 00:04:01.800
I'll take them.

00:04:02.140 --> 00:04:03.220
No, I'll...

00:04:03.520 --> 00:04:06.020
Don't worry! Just leave it to me!

00:04:21.080 --> 00:04:22.420
Thanks.

00:04:22.420 --> 00:04:24.610
Tell your uncle I said hi.

00:04:24.810 --> 00:04:25.610
Okay!

00:04:28.920 --> 00:04:29.850
Bye now!

00:04:32.090 --> 00:04:34.040
Oh, was that...

00:04:34.040 --> 00:04:37.210
Yeah, that's Ex, the boy who
 lives just outside of town.

00:04:37.660 --> 00:04:40.230
He's sure grown...

00:04:41.760 --> 00:04:44.510
He's a "role-less" with no fate, right?

00:04:44.950 --> 00:04:46.970
Don't bring that up.

00:04:47.420 --> 00:04:49.720
But it's true, isn't it?

00:04:49.950 --> 00:04:51.490
Forget about him.

00:04:51.490 --> 00:04:55.880
Your book says a good man is gonna 
fall for you next year, right?

00:04:55.880 --> 00:04:58.110
Learn to cook something already.

00:04:59.140 --> 00:05:00.730
Just leave it to me.

00:05:02.240 --> 00:05:04.120
It's the prince's carriage!

00:05:04.780 --> 00:05:06.090
There! There it is!

00:05:13.280 --> 00:05:17.210
Aww... I didn't get to see 
the prince today, either.

00:05:17.210 --> 00:05:19.130
I wonder just how amazing he is...

00:05:19.130 --> 00:05:20.960
I'd love to meet him.

00:05:23.300 --> 00:05:24.510
It's Ex!

00:05:24.510 --> 00:05:27.300
What do you want, role-less?

00:05:27.640 --> 00:05:29.300
I came to deliver some pumpkins...

00:05:30.610 --> 00:05:32.260
Poor kid.

00:05:32.260 --> 00:05:33.310
Look!

00:05:33.310 --> 00:05:36.890
I'm gonna be a castle guard!

00:05:37.130 --> 00:05:38.980
You're jealous, right?

00:05:39.280 --> 00:05:42.150
Idiot. Nobody but you can read that, you know?

00:05:42.150 --> 00:05:43.150
Oh, right.

00:05:46.070 --> 00:05:47.400
Leaving already?

00:05:47.400 --> 00:05:49.410
You're no fun!

00:05:55.110 --> 00:06:00.130
<i>But really, why is my Book of Fate blank?</i>

00:06:00.130 --> 00:06:02.790
You can't even do laundry?

00:06:03.340 --> 00:06:06.340
My sheets are still filthy.

00:06:06.750 --> 00:06:09.840
I'm sorry. I'll wash them again right away.

00:06:10.070 --> 00:06:12.180
You really are useless.

00:06:14.000 --> 00:06:18.150
Mother, I'd like to try on a new dress!

00:06:18.150 --> 00:06:19.350
Could I?

00:06:19.350 --> 00:06:20.270
Me, too!

00:06:20.270 --> 00:06:21.700
Of course.

00:06:27.210 --> 00:06:28.510
Cinderella!

00:06:36.710 --> 00:06:40.250
Are your new mom and sisters
 always like that?

00:06:40.530 --> 00:06:41.500
Yeah.

00:06:41.500 --> 00:06:43.130
I see...

00:06:43.560 --> 00:06:46.880
Things sure were nice when
 my real mother was alive...

00:06:54.160 --> 00:06:55.850
What about you, Ex?

00:06:55.850 --> 00:06:59.810
O-Oh, yeah... I went to 
my parents' graves this morning.

00:06:59.810 --> 00:07:02.910
No, I mean your aunt and uncle...

00:07:04.990 --> 00:07:07.910
They don't abuse me, but...

00:07:08.750 --> 00:07:09.740
But?

00:07:10.020 --> 00:07:12.700
It feels like they're scared of me.

00:07:22.440 --> 00:07:24.000
I'm so jealous of birds...

00:07:24.000 --> 00:07:25.390
Because they can fly?

00:07:27.220 --> 00:07:30.220
Because they can go wherever they want.

00:07:31.210 --> 00:07:32.480
Yeah...

00:07:34.360 --> 00:07:35.750
I know what you mean.

00:07:37.970 --> 00:07:42.480
But you're not like me, Cinderella! 
You've got a great fate awaiting you, right?

00:07:42.480 --> 00:07:45.230
What happens when you turn sixteen again?

00:07:45.490 --> 00:07:46.710
Um...

00:07:49.030 --> 00:07:54.570
When I turn sixteen,
 I'll go to a ball at the castle, and...

00:07:54.570 --> 00:07:59.830
You'll dance with the prince, marry him
 and live happily ever after, right?

00:08:00.160 --> 00:08:02.380
You do remember!

00:08:02.380 --> 00:08:04.690
You told me a bunch of times.

00:08:05.900 --> 00:08:07.040
But...

00:08:07.790 --> 00:08:13.050
I just can't believe what my book says
 is really going to happen.

00:08:13.610 --> 00:08:17.050
Sometimes I feel like I'm going 
to spend the rest of my life

00:08:17.050 --> 00:08:21.880
sleeping next to the fire, 
covered in cinders.

00:08:22.350 --> 00:08:25.100
If your Book of Fate says so,
 it'll come true.

00:08:25.900 --> 00:08:26.980
But...

00:08:27.210 --> 00:08:29.480
Okay, I know what I'll do!

00:08:29.810 --> 00:08:34.240
Since I don't have a role anyway, 
I'll help make your fate come true.

00:08:34.240 --> 00:08:36.490
From now on, that'll be my role!

00:08:36.860 --> 00:08:38.870
Thank you, Ex!

00:08:41.180 --> 00:08:44.320
<i>But... what can I do?</i>

00:08:49.090 --> 00:08:51.960
Hey, honey. About Ex...

00:08:51.960 --> 00:08:53.880
Yeah, I know.

00:08:53.880 --> 00:08:57.680
I don't know how to handle a role-less.

00:08:57.680 --> 00:09:00.970
Once he's old enough to strike out 
on his own, I'll talk to him.

00:09:00.970 --> 00:09:03.020
Just another two or three more years.

00:09:03.020 --> 00:09:04.480
You'd better.

00:09:14.370 --> 00:09:15.240
It's so cold!

00:09:15.240 --> 00:09:16.950
Put some more wood on the fire!

00:09:16.950 --> 00:09:18.520
Right away!

00:09:19.870 --> 00:09:24.540
My darlings, we'll be going to get you
 fitted for new dresses tomorrow.

00:09:24.540 --> 00:09:25.830
Really?

00:09:25.830 --> 00:09:28.670
The ones you have now are out of style.

00:09:28.670 --> 00:09:30.590
Thank you, Mother!

00:09:30.860 --> 00:09:33.130
You're so lucky, Cinderella.

00:09:33.130 --> 00:09:36.220
You never have to worry about fashion.

00:09:44.650 --> 00:09:45.870
Using cinders for makeup?

00:09:45.870 --> 00:09:47.310
It looks great on you!

00:09:47.310 --> 00:09:50.230
That's enough, you two.

00:09:50.510 --> 00:09:51.810
Yes, ma'am!

00:09:53.690 --> 00:09:55.040
<i>It's okay...</i>

00:09:55.850 --> 00:09:58.480
<i>Once I turn sixteen, it'll all be okay.</i>

00:10:05.600 --> 00:10:08.450
How old is this? It's covered in dust.

00:10:10.560 --> 00:10:13.000
Uncle, where's the spare hoe?

00:10:17.510 --> 00:10:18.900
A wooden sword?

00:11:23.570 --> 00:11:24.490
I brought your pumpkins.

00:11:24.490 --> 00:11:26.160
Get a hold of yourself.

00:11:26.390 --> 00:11:30.460
But my Book of Fate didn't 
say anything about this...

00:11:31.170 --> 00:11:32.670
Is something the matter?

00:11:32.670 --> 00:11:38.380
She says her husband was attacked 
by a weird monster in the forest...

00:11:38.380 --> 00:11:40.010
A weird monster?

00:11:40.010 --> 00:11:44.680
Fortunately it seems he'll survive, 
but his wounds are serious.

00:11:44.680 --> 00:11:46.350
I'm sorry to hear that.

00:11:46.350 --> 00:11:47.970
I don't want your sympathy!

00:11:48.210 --> 00:11:51.230
You don't even have a fate!
 What would you know?!

00:11:51.580 --> 00:11:53.310
Hey, cut that out.

00:11:59.380 --> 00:12:02.030
No, don't mind me.

00:12:07.780 --> 00:12:10.330
This is a lively town.

00:12:11.750 --> 00:12:13.250
Pardon me.

00:12:13.260 --> 00:12:16.660
I'm just a traveling performer.

00:12:18.310 --> 00:12:21.920
There's going to be a joyous festival 
here in the city tonight,

00:12:21.920 --> 00:12:25.340
and a splendid ball at the castle.

00:12:25.700 --> 00:12:26.970
A ball?

00:12:26.970 --> 00:12:28.010
Indeed.

00:12:29.430 --> 00:12:32.850
I put extra effort into my preparations.

00:12:32.850 --> 00:12:36.360
I guarantee it will be unforgettable.

00:12:39.050 --> 00:12:40.110
Ex?

00:12:51.620 --> 00:12:54.710
I see. So the ball is tonight.

00:12:54.710 --> 00:12:55.370
Yes.

00:12:55.620 --> 00:12:57.250
Congratulations, Cinderella.

00:12:57.510 --> 00:13:01.050
I only made it this far because 
you were there to cheer me up.

00:13:01.050 --> 00:13:02.130
Really?

00:13:02.300 --> 00:13:07.300
Really. Without you, I would've 
run away from that house.

00:13:09.980 --> 00:13:12.470
Anyway, it's not time to celebrate yet.

00:13:12.470 --> 00:13:16.150
I'm just meeting the prince tonight 
and dancing with him.

00:13:16.440 --> 00:13:21.110
But later he'll come to discover
 the owner of the glass slipper

00:13:21.110 --> 00:13:23.490
and you get to see him again, right?

00:13:23.880 --> 00:13:24.690
Yes.

00:13:25.760 --> 00:13:30.240
I can still hardly believe my life's
 going to change tonight.

00:13:30.240 --> 00:13:33.250
Don't worry! It'll go great!

00:13:33.250 --> 00:13:34.500
I guarantee it!

00:13:36.790 --> 00:13:37.750
Ex!

00:13:37.990 --> 00:13:39.250
Oh, right...

00:13:39.430 --> 00:13:43.960
You said before that your Fairy Godmother 
uses magic to turn mice into horses...

00:13:44.220 --> 00:13:45.760
And a pumpkin into a carriage!

00:13:46.030 --> 00:13:47.510
So use this!

00:13:49.800 --> 00:13:51.010
Ex!

00:13:51.260 --> 00:13:53.640
Well, come on. You'd better hurry home

00:13:53.640 --> 00:13:57.140
or else you'll miss your Fairy Godmother.

00:13:57.360 --> 00:13:58.440
Yeah, you're right!

00:13:58.440 --> 00:14:00.200
Thank you, Ex!

00:14:08.840 --> 00:14:09.910
I'm home.

00:14:09.910 --> 00:14:11.280
You're late.

00:14:11.280 --> 00:14:12.280
Sorry.

00:14:12.280 --> 00:14:14.310
We need to talk.

00:14:15.540 --> 00:14:18.670
About your future...

00:14:19.510 --> 00:14:20.430
Sorry.

00:14:21.360 --> 00:14:22.620
Can it wait until tomorrow?

00:14:22.620 --> 00:14:25.630
Y-Yeah, that's okay.

00:14:25.630 --> 00:14:26.780
Goodnight, then.

00:14:33.920 --> 00:14:38.690
<i>Once Cinderella and the prince are wed, 
my role will be fulfilled.</i>

00:14:39.070 --> 00:14:41.580
<i>What do I do then?</i>

00:15:10.140 --> 00:15:11.180
What's that...?

00:15:17.430 --> 00:15:18.830
What?

00:15:22.650 --> 00:15:23.930
A monster?!

00:15:26.690 --> 00:15:28.400
What are you doing? Run away!

00:15:28.400 --> 00:15:29.640
Run?

00:15:33.670 --> 00:15:35.870
I can handle them myself!

00:15:35.870 --> 00:15:36.830
Get out of here!

00:15:37.450 --> 00:15:39.200
I can't do that!

00:15:51.230 --> 00:15:52.180
Why...

00:15:52.660 --> 00:15:55.600
I was never given a role in the first place.

00:15:56.040 --> 00:15:57.850
The least I can do is save someone!

00:15:57.850 --> 00:15:59.790
Never given a role?

00:15:59.790 --> 00:16:00.600
Don't tell me...

00:16:02.550 --> 00:16:03.850
Come at me!

00:16:03.850 --> 00:16:04.790
Wait!

00:16:05.520 --> 00:16:07.460
Take this Bookmark of Guidance,

00:16:07.460 --> 00:16:11.110
put it in your blank Book of Fate, and shout...

00:16:11.430 --> 00:16:12.360
"Connect!"

00:16:13.600 --> 00:16:15.370
"Connect"?

00:16:17.700 --> 00:16:18.850
Connect!

00:16:27.640 --> 00:16:30.090
H-Huh? Wh-What is this?

00:16:30.090 --> 00:16:31.300
What happened to me?

00:16:32.220 --> 00:16:34.220
I've got a real sword,

00:16:34.220 --> 00:16:35.850
and even armor!

00:16:40.390 --> 00:16:42.270
My body moved on its own...

00:16:42.270 --> 00:16:44.520
That's right! That's the connection!

00:16:44.520 --> 00:16:47.690
You've connected with the soul of a hero!

00:16:58.690 --> 00:17:01.660
<i>It's like the monsters have slowed down.</i>

00:17:05.160 --> 00:17:06.960
What is all this...?

00:17:13.840 --> 00:17:16.430
Can you save your astonishment 
for later and help me?

00:17:17.280 --> 00:17:18.250
Sorry!

00:17:27.400 --> 00:17:28.730
You saved me.

00:17:28.730 --> 00:17:31.340
I never got your name, though.

00:17:32.040 --> 00:17:33.030
Ex.

00:17:33.030 --> 00:17:35.030
I see. I'm Reina.

00:17:35.030 --> 00:17:39.490
Um, Reina, there's a lot I'd like to ask you...

00:17:39.490 --> 00:17:40.280
About what?

00:17:40.280 --> 00:17:41.370
Everything!

00:17:41.370 --> 00:17:45.000
Those monsters, this strange power...

00:17:45.480 --> 00:17:47.310
I think it's best I not answer.

00:17:47.770 --> 00:17:48.960
But why?

00:17:48.960 --> 00:17:51.050
You can keep that bookmark.

00:17:51.050 --> 00:17:53.460
There's no telling when 
the villains will return.

00:17:53.990 --> 00:17:58.090
I see... So those monsters 
are called villains.

00:17:59.210 --> 00:18:02.410
Well then, I'm headed to the castle.

00:18:03.440 --> 00:18:04.430
Reina.

00:18:04.430 --> 00:18:05.560
I said I won't answer...

00:18:05.560 --> 00:18:07.120
That's the wrong way.

00:18:15.320 --> 00:18:17.320
Hurry, hurry!

00:18:17.480 --> 00:18:19.620
That's the eight o'clock bell!

00:18:19.620 --> 00:18:21.950
The ball's already starting!

00:18:21.950 --> 00:18:26.250
It's slow Cinderella's fault that
 it took us forever to get changed.

00:18:26.770 --> 00:18:28.090
I'm sorry...

00:18:29.060 --> 00:18:32.750
See you later, lovely little Cinderella.

00:18:33.160 --> 00:18:35.510
Make sure you get
 this place spotless, you hear?

00:18:38.580 --> 00:18:42.450
<i>When will my Fairy Godmother come?</i>

00:18:43.080 --> 00:18:46.140
I was actually on my way to the castle, too.

00:18:46.140 --> 00:18:48.530
I see. That's great news.

00:18:48.530 --> 00:18:50.890
I just arrived in this Story Zone.

00:18:50.890 --> 00:18:52.180
Story Zone?

00:18:53.730 --> 00:18:55.860
I guess I'll tell you just a little.

00:18:55.860 --> 00:18:57.670
You know who the Storyteller is, right?

00:18:57.670 --> 00:19:01.280
Yeah. That's the god who wrote 
everyone's fates, right?

00:19:01.290 --> 00:19:06.370
A Story Zone is a space 
created by the Storyteller.

00:19:07.710 --> 00:19:11.380
Story Zones are based on ancient legends.

00:19:11.380 --> 00:19:15.170
And those within a Story Zone 
are assigned a role,

00:19:15.610 --> 00:19:19.710
written down in a book 
that only they can read.

00:19:20.880 --> 00:19:23.390
But not everybody gets one.

00:19:24.120 --> 00:19:29.000
You knew my Book of Fate was blank, right?

00:19:29.000 --> 00:19:31.810
And you said you just got to this Story Zone.

00:19:32.060 --> 00:19:33.650
So where did you come from, then?

00:19:33.650 --> 00:19:36.530
Why are you going to the castle?

00:19:36.530 --> 00:19:37.860
I'm looking for the main character.

00:19:38.310 --> 00:19:39.280
Main character?

00:19:39.610 --> 00:19:43.370
The person you could think of 
as the face of the Story Zone.

00:19:43.370 --> 00:19:46.360
The hero who saves his people, for instance.

00:19:46.360 --> 00:19:48.790
Or the princess of mysterious birth.

00:19:49.110 --> 00:19:53.260
I figured a castle in the center of town
 would be a good place to look for clues.

00:19:54.610 --> 00:19:55.870
Is that...

00:20:02.400 --> 00:20:04.850
Cinderella! Cinderella!

00:20:05.510 --> 00:20:07.220
Is that you, Fairy Godmother?!

00:20:11.950 --> 00:20:13.980
Yes, it's me.

00:20:15.260 --> 00:20:17.400
You really came!

00:20:17.670 --> 00:20:22.400
You're going to a ball. 
We can't have you weeping like that.

00:20:30.640 --> 00:20:32.790
Is that really me?

00:20:32.790 --> 00:20:34.170
That's not all. Behold!

00:20:38.420 --> 00:20:39.800
How lovely!

00:20:40.060 --> 00:20:42.300
The glass slippers I've been dreaming of!

00:20:44.000 --> 00:20:47.050
Now all you need is a carriage 
to take you to the castle.

00:20:55.350 --> 00:20:56.810
Please use this!

00:20:58.020 --> 00:20:59.820
You're all set, huh?

00:21:03.820 --> 00:21:05.800
This is just hypothetical,

00:21:05.800 --> 00:21:09.830
but what if there were a girl who'd 
spent her whole life suffering,

00:21:10.320 --> 00:21:12.410
waiting for the prince to fall in love with her?

00:21:12.890 --> 00:21:17.630
Someone with a Book of Fate like that 
would probably be a main character, yes.

00:21:17.910 --> 00:21:19.480
Then Cinderella...

00:21:19.480 --> 00:21:23.590
Cinderella must be the main character 
of this world. No, this Story Zone.

00:21:23.880 --> 00:21:27.390
If this Cinderella girl really 
is the main character,

00:21:27.390 --> 00:21:28.220
she's in danger.

00:21:29.260 --> 00:21:33.230
The Chaos Teller is almost always 
lurking near the main character.

00:21:33.490 --> 00:21:34.750
Hang on...

00:21:34.750 --> 00:21:36.230
What's a Chaos Teller?

00:21:36.530 --> 00:21:38.610
A creature that destroys Story Zones.

00:21:55.530 --> 00:21:57.330
Be careful, Cinderella.

00:21:57.330 --> 00:22:01.840
The magic spell I cast on you will end
 when the clock strikes midnight.

00:22:01.840 --> 00:22:03.840
Yes, I know!

00:22:04.320 --> 00:22:06.340
Have a wonderful night, then.

00:22:17.110 --> 00:22:20.270
Good evening, everyone!

00:22:20.270 --> 00:22:22.900
And what a wonderful evening it will be!

00:22:24.200 --> 00:22:30.430
Let us begin our ball at 
 this beautiful castle!

00:22:32.290 --> 00:22:35.100
Cinderella!
